      "ja": "Shanghai DS®CAFE Brand Design"
    },
    "summary": {
      "en": "Dasheng® Coffee is located in Dasheng Hutong on Huashan Road in Shanghai, taking the name \"Dasheng\" to mean the coffee born in Dasheng Hutong. Dasheng Hutong is one of the few lanes in Shanghai called \"Hutong\", originally established by the Belgian Catholic Church as a property of the Universalist Community in Shanghai, and built between 1912 and 1936 by Father Drummond. The property was named after the \"hutong\" commonly used in the north because the priest was from Beijing.",
      "zh": "Dasheng® Coffee is located in Dasheng Hutong on Huashan Road in Shanghai, taking the name \"Dasheng\" to mean the coffee born in Dasheng Hutong. Dasheng Hutong is one of the few lanes in Shanghai called \"Hutong\", originally established by the Belgian Catholic Church as a property of the Universalist Community in Shanghai, and built between 1912 and 1936 by Father Drummond. The property was named after the \"hutong\" commonly used in the north because the priest was from Beijing.",
      "ja": "Dasheng® Coffee is located in Dasheng Hutong on Huashan Road in Shanghai, taking the name \"Dasheng\" to mean the coffee born in Dasheng Hutong. Dasheng Hutong is one of the few lanes in Shanghai called \"Hutong\", originally established by the Belgian Catholic Church as a property of the Universalist Community in Shanghai, and built between 1912 and 1936 by Father Drummond. The property was named after the \"hutong\" commonly used in the north because the priest was from Beijing."
    },
